  "content_text_24": "Four teams account for 61% of first-year exits",
  "content_text_25": ": Support Hyderabad, Support Bengaluru, Field Ops West and Sales SMB. Across those teams, first-year attrition rose from 18.2% to 26.4% in the two quarters after the rotating shift pattern started in January. The rise is concentrated in employees who received three or more shift changes with under 72 hours' notice. Teams on the same pattern with stable rosters show no increase, so ",
  "content_text_26": "the pattern itself is not the driver — the notice period is",
  "content_text_27": ".",
  "content_text_28": "Evidence Base: 1,284 employee records, 41,220 shift assignments, 218 exit records (Jan 2025 – Sep 2026). Confidence: ",
  "content_text_29": "HIGH",
